---
title: Kerala Egg Curry
servings: 2
-- yields:
tags:
  - entres
source:
  name: Kannamma Cooks
  url: https://www.kannammacooks.com/egg-curry-coconut-milk/
-- introduction: 
---

= Gravy

Melt @ghee{2%tbsp} in a pot.

Fry @curry leaves{12} in the ghee until the leaves turn darker.\
> about 1 sprig

Add @./cook/bhuna-masala{4%oz} and continue to fry until thickens a little.

Turn off heat Add @cardamom pods{2}(ground), @cloves{3}(ground), and @fennel seeds{0.5%tsp}(ground).\
> The ground spices can easily burn, the original recipes calls for these to be whole spices, added before / with the curry leaves. A lot of people don't like having the whole spices in there, and I don't like fishing them out, so this is an attempt to mitigate that.

Add @coconut milk{1%cup} a few seconds after adding the spices and turn the heat back on.

Add @turmeric{1/2%tsp}(ground), @Kashmiri red chili{1/2%tsp}(ground), @black pepper{1/2%tsp}(ground), @garam masala{1/2%tsp}, and @coriander{1%tbsp}(ground).

Cook on low heat for another {10%minutes}, add water to reach desired consistency.

Use an #immersion blender{} to blend to smoother consistency if desired.

= Eggs

Boil @./cook/boiled-eggs{4} to your desired consistency.

Once peeled, make a few small slits in them for the gravy to infiltrate.

= Tadka

Heat @oil{1%tbsp} in a small skillet or wok (ghee, coconut oil, etc.).

Add @shallots{2%tbsp}(sliced) and @curry leaves{12}, fry until shallots are golden.

Add to the gravy.

= Serving

Once tadka is added to the gravy, add the eggs and let simmer for a few minutes before serving.